<section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <h2 id="faq-title">Questions about Twine</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need an account? Where does my data live?</summary>
      <p>No account. Your highlights live on your devices and in your private iCloud database. Twine doesn't send your library to the developer. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains website lookups, optional diagnostics, support messages and connected AI tools.</p>
    </details>
    {%- if site.pricing %}
    {% include "draft/pricing-faq.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}
    <details id="faq-ai-tools">
      <summary>Which AI tools can connect to Twine?</summary>
      <p>Use a compatible tool on your Mac that supports local MCP servers over HTTP with bearer-token authentication. Cloud-hosted chat services can't reach Twine, because it only listens on your Mac. Some tools need a connector or config file; see the <a href="/docs#connect-an-ai-tool">connection guide</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can an AI tool change my highlights?</summary>
      <p>No. AI Access is read-only. Tools can search, list, read, and export your highlights, but can't add, edit, or delete them through this connection. A tool with the token can read your whole library; turn AI Access off or replace the token to revoke access.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need Apple Intelligence?</summary>
      <p>Only to write or refresh on-device AI context. You can read a note synced from another device without generating it again. Highlighting, the library, sync, and AI Access all work without it.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-iphone-sync">
      <summary>When do highlights sync between my devices?</summary>
      <p>On Mac, highlights sync while Twine is running. On iPhone, highlights made in Safari sync the next time you open Twine. Select text and tap Twine in Safari's page menu, then open the app to upload. Use the same Apple Account on both devices; see the <a href="/docs#sync-with-icloud">sync guide</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-browsers">
      <summary>Does Twine work in other browsers?</summary>
      <p>Twine is built for Safari. Chrome, other Chromium browsers, and Firefox aren't supported in this release.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-private-browsing">
      <summary>Does Twine work in Private Browsing?</summary>
      <p>No. Twine doesn't save or show highlights in Private Browsing.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it work on every web page?</summary>
      <p>It works on standard web pages with selectable text and permission to run in Safari. Twine leaves text fields alone. If a page's text or surrounding context changes, the highlight may not reappear on the page, but it stays in your library.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Are there limits?</summary>
      <p>A single highlight can be up to 5,000 characters, with up to 500 highlights per page. Twine saves up to 30 new highlights a minute; auto-highlight on Mac skips selections over 1,000 characters.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which devices and languages does Twine support?</summary>
      <p>Mac with macOS {{ site.macOS }} and iPhone with iOS {{ site.iOS }}. Twine is available in English, German, Spanish, French, and Russian. See the <a href="#requirements">system requirements</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I get help?</summary>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. Twine is made by one developer, and you'll hear back from him directly. There is no live chat or guaranteed response time. You can also read the <a href="/docs">docs</a>, <a href="{{ site.feedbackUrl }}">send public feedback on GitHub</a>, or visit <a href="/support">support</a>.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

